      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need some help writing a rejection email. We had a candidate who made it all the way to the final round for a Senior DevOps Engineer position here in our Austin office, but we decided to go with someone else. They were actually really strong technically and had great culture fit, so I want to keep the door open for future roles without sounding fake. Can you help me draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you craft a rejection email that's both honest and gracious. You want to acknowledge the candidate's impressive technical skills and cultural alignment, while also being clear about your decision to move forward with another candidate. Here's a draft to get you started:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior DevOps Engineer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your technical expertise and your alignment with our company culture, which is a rare find in our pool of candidates. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience better align with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the prospect of having you join our team. Your passion for DevOps and your ability to think critically about complex problems are truly impressive. We were also impressed by your enthusiasm for our company culture and your willingness to learn and grow with us.\n\nAlthough we won't be moving forward with your application at this time, we would love to keep the door open for future opportunities. We often find that our best candidates are those who have been with us for a while, and we'd love to have you back on board if",
