      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior DevOps Engineer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your technical expertise and your alignment with our company culture, which is a rare find in our pool of candidates. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience better align with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the prospect of having you join our team. Your passion for DevOps and your ability to think critically about complex problems are truly impressive. We were also impressed by your enthusiasm for our company culture and your willingness to learn and grow with us.\n\nAlthough we won't be moving forward with your application at this time, we would love to keep the door open for future opportunities. We often find that our best candidates are those who have been with us for a while, and we'd love to have you back on board if the right fit arises again. In the meantime, we'd like to keep your resume on file for specific future openings in our infrastructure team, particularly if we're looking for someone with your expertise in [specific area of expertise]. We",
